{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791117887,"nonce":"u9ZMLiCC+z2cO30vaFg0cTLsJhs=","title":"Text layout ignores letter-spacing, so letter-spaced centred text sits off centre","message":"Layout measures text from blinc_layout's TextMeasureContext, which at the pinned Blinc revision (6accf69) has no letter_spacing; the renderer draws with the node's letter-spacing. Text with negative tracking draws narrower than its layout box, so centred text shifts left by (characters - 1) x spacing / 2.\n\nMeasured with tools/snapshot/scenes/AlignScene.hx (ashui.debug.AlignProbe), buttons with letter-spacing: var(--tracking-tight):\n- \"Login with Email\": ink 16.5px from the left edge, 22px from the right (dx -2.7)\n- \"Outline\", \"running\": dx -1.2\n\nWorked around by dropping letter-spacing from .ui-button, .ui-tabs-trigger and .ui-toggle; afterwards every probed label is within 0.5px of centre. Inputs, selects, menu shortcuts and sidebar group labels keep theirs: they are left-aligned, so only their right edge is off.\n\nFix:\n1. Blinc commit 57aedd40 (\"fix(layout): carry letter-spacing into the measure context\") adds TextMeasureContext.letter_spacing. It is local to the Blinc checkout and not yet on Blinc's main; once it is, bump blinc in Cargo.lock.\n2. In blinc_abi, set the context's letter_spacing when LetterSpacing is written (layout_router.rs, the P::LetterSpacing render write; record_text it as font_size is) and on unset.\n3. Restore letter-spacing: var(--tracking-tight) on the three rules and re-run AlignScene.","files":null}]}